Chapter Two
Agricultural Inputs.
Crop seed and propagating materials are the most important inputs among the
basic elements of crop production. We can produce crop year by year using
these inputs. Besides, using these inputs, we can also acclimatize a new crop in
a country, conserve genetic characteristics of a crop and improve a crop by
applying biotechnology
